 the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}) & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & ={e}^{c}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we let ${e}^{c}={r}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surfaces form a family of spheres centered at the origin." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338965 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186338505 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338965 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71596" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338965 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338965 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the equation of the level surface for the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+3(y-1)^{2}-{z}^{2}$ that passes through the point $P(4,2,1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338965 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8ee763a3-710a-5e1f-a2ce-e98f8f8714e0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338965 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the value of the function at $P$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(4,2,1) & ={4}^{2}+3(2-1)^{2}-{1}^{2}=18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=18.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}+3(y-1)^{2}-{z}^{2} & =18 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{18}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{6}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{18} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface that passes through the point $P(4,2,1)$ is the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{18}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{6}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{18}=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403482 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403483 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403482 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71582" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403482 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403482 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following describes the $c$-level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}},$ where $c>0?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403482 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "196e54b1-6877-5611-9d9d-7ecb8d24abce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403482 #edb/ref 1074 "The level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}} & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2} & ={c}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get a family of hyperboloids of one sheet:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1,\\,c\\in (0,\\infty ).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403483 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403484 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403483 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403483 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403483 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403483 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403488 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403483 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403483 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403483 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186403484 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403483 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b461523f-a59b-5dc6-8f0b-36ed850f9a53" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403484 #edb/ref 1080 "A family of hyperboloids of one sheet: $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403484 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403484 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ec4a428d-e3d3-5679-bb8f-d50463ce62ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403485 #edb/ref 1080 "A family of hyperboloids of one sheet: $cx-2cy+3cz-8=0$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403485 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403485 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cf4cbec1-86a0-549a-8343-60b68cea6056" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403486 #edb/ref 1080 "A family of hyperbolic paraboloid: $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^